{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076056-how-to-get-the-watchtowers-to-be-part-of-the-active-story-not-just-of-the-past","id":1076056,"title":"How to get the Watchtowers to be part of the active story not just of the past","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-10T12:54:15-07:00","id":1076056,"title":"How to get the Watchtowers to be part of the active story not just of the past","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> i'd like to start a MTA campaign, but I don't have any experience as its extrem unfamiliarly in my region.<br /> In the campaign i'd like to integrate all the awaking story /journey/travel and the involved experience strongly, all the stuff that happened before the character reaches its tower and there \u201cwithin\u201d. As From my point of view the event of awaking is to much happening and should make to much with a charakter, then to just us during preludium.<br /> But I have no good idea how to this. I thought about developing the story on the run during play,like flashbacks and so on. for written story this would be a common method, but this can hardly be done with an outcome-open rpg. As when we start playing at least the player should know what has happened during his or her awakening.<br /> <br /> As I'm sure I'm not the only one with this idea, maybe someone here can share his or her approach?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13256-flotsch","name":"Flotsch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:08:47-07:00","id":1076061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flotsch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1076056-how-to-get-the-watchtowers-to-be-part-of-the-active-story-not-just-of-the-past#post1076056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello,<br /> <br /> i'd like to start a MTA campaign, but I don't have any experience as its extrem unfamiliarly in my region.<br /> In the campaign i'd like to integrate all the awaking story /journey/travel and the involved experience strongly, all the stuff that happened before the character reaches its tower and there \u201cwithin\u201d. As From my point of view the event of awaking is to much happening and should make to much with a charakter, then to just us during preludium.<br /> But I have no good idea how to this. I thought about developing the story on the run during play,like flashbacks and so on. for written story this would be a common method, but this can hardly be done with an outcome-open rpg. As when we start playing at least the player should know what has happened during his or her awakening.<br /> <br /> As I'm sure I'm not the only one with this idea, maybe someone here can share his or her approach?<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the forums.<br /> <br /> As far as the player knowing their Awakening, you could borrow a page from Mummy and build it out during play, like you suggest - the only thing certain is that they did awaken. You could include themes, events, or Supernal Entities from their Awakening showing up in &quot;real time&quot; play. And remember that Mystery Plays (the Awakening overlaying real events) is a thing - maybe the Demon you conquered, or Fae you bargained with was actually someone else, and now the consequences have come due.<br /> <br /> And, while not a good idea for someone just starting out, you could always leave the conclusion of the Awakening uncertain - such as if the character instead became a Banisher. (Problem with that one is the issues with Wisdom vs Integrity)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:41:01-07:00","id":1076158,"title":"","content":"Yeah, playing the Mystery Play version of Awakenings sounds fun. It also allows you to transition from mortal-level game, where you familiarize yourself with the ChroD world in general, and to Mage-level game, where the real fun begins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:01:22-07:00","id":1076167,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, it's actually <i>not</i> guaranteed that characters fully recall what happened during their Mystery Play. Remember, your Mystery Play is a grand exposure to cosmic Truth, in which your soul has departed your body and entered the Supernal. Such things have a dream-like quality and, once the new Mage returns to their body, fully Awakened, all that Truth has to be filtered by a mortal mind. It gets compressed; twisted into a form that can be understood. The full sensation of touching the Supernal is, thereafter, lost to the Awakened save in the highest of visions and the rush of casting a spell.<br /> <br /> As a Mage's Gnosis rises, the smaller details might start to return in dreams and sudden recollections, but, until such a time, it's entirely reasonable all they recall is the broadest strokes and a few critical details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:59:51-07:00","id":1076207,"title":"","content":"I am a little shocked that there are not more players who want their characters to obsess over the Watchtowers. although for me I usually have my character(s) assume there are no Oracles and that the Watchtowers are their own entities, but that might be because I dabbled a little in Wicca as a kid and am kinda biased. It sounds like a very awesome idea, though. Any time I ST'd for anyone, the thing I always looked forward to doing was their Prelude. I don't understand why anyone would want to skip something so engaging. The symbols and events of the Awakening play so neatly into future mysteries and biases.<br /> <br /> Plus, there is the fact that the road to Ascension is its own Mystery Play, with it being nearly invisible prior to becoming an Archmage, but I still like the idea of using call-backs from the Awakening in the game. A Prelate out to get you because you crossed a minion of the Exarchs in the supernal, doing a summoning and getting an entity you met during your Awakening, finding a Supernal Artifact that looks like something you saw in the Awakening, things like that. Something or anything to make your new magical life really magical and meaningful--and dangerous. Or at least alluring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:11:22-07:00","id":1076216,"title":"","content":"It seems the upcoming supplement, Signs of Sorcery, will deal with Mysteries directly from the Supernal Worlds. Which will probably include Awakenings, the Watchtowers, and maybe Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T01:55:19-07:00","id":1076371,"title":"","content":"At our table we tend to use the Awakening as a way to figure out a character's drives as a Mage, so the event may be in the past but it creates a focus for where they're going in the future. For instance, an Acanthus that manages to trick a Fae king out of his throne will spend his time focusing on the use of magic to derive authority in the Fallen (Carving out his own kingdom) and explore the repercussions of &quot;ruling&quot; a realm of Arcadia at remove since he can't go back except via ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:47:57-07:00","id":1078082,"title":"","content":"Well personally i really gravitated to the idea of watchtowers in the game.<br /> <br /> The lore on them is huge for the 5 in the supernal...but what i really liked was the idea that others might exist.<br /> <br /> So....when i ran a HUGE larp the overarching plot was leading up to the players finding an abyssal watchtower being constructed. So honestly if you want another way for people to get up close and personal with one that is one way. You then can twist their wonder and obsessions over watchtowers to become something of horror to this thing that might change the very nature of magic in a way that is irreparable.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13276-bristark","name":"Bristark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13276_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}